    "final_message": "The acceptance test now passes, and `scripts/verify story-drafting` is green: tessercheck with zero findings, `mypy --strict` clean over 77 files, 80 tests in the tiers below the root, and the root test through the served host. The test file is unchanged from the last commit. Everything is committed on the branch as `c6f64b6`.\n\n**How a run works now:**\n1. The `RunOrchestrator` workflow saves the run at stage `drafting`, so it can be read back while stories are being written.\n2. It asks a new `StoryActions` service to write stories for the job. That service sits behind one port, `StoryWriter`.\n3. It hands the stories to the run as a `Draft`. The new `Run.drafted` step moves the run from `drafting` to `awaiting_pick` and leaves nothing accepted. It refuses a run that is not drafting, and `Draft` refuses an empty draft.\n4. It saves the drafted run again, then waits on the `pick_story` durable promise.\n\n**Choosing the language model:** the component reads a `STORY_WRITER` setting, and a missing or unknown value is an error when the app starts.\n- `canned` is the deterministic writer. `scripts/verify` sets it for the tests and the host.\n- `anthropic` drafts with `claude-opus-5-5` and asks for the stories back as JSON. It needs `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` and refuses to start without one.\n- The Anthropic adapter's test runs against a fake Messages API in `story-drafting/simulated/`. The analyzer skips that folder, so no test calls a real model.\n\n**Things you should know:**\n- **No way to resolve the pick yet.** Making the pick is out of scope, so nothing can resolve the promise. Runs started by the root test stay waiting on your Restate server; that is the state the story asks for. The workflow, dispatcher and context tests kill the runs they leave waiting.\n- **A refused request stalls the run.** If the model stops without finishing, the adapter returns no stories and the domain refuses the empty draft. Restate then retries and pauses the run after 5 attempts.\n- **No automatic fall"
  },
